1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,000
1,800 years ago, dumplings weren't food.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,400
Legend says a doctor made them as medicine.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,800
Wrapped lamb and herbs to warm frostbitten ears.

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,200
He shaped them like little ears — "tender ears."

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,600
The word jiaozi echoes "the turn of the year."

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,000
So families eat them at New Year's midnight.

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,400
Their shape? Old silver ingots — a wish for wealth.

9
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,800
Double-tap if you'd fold a batch tonight.

10
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:23,800
★ Expert Tip: pleat the edge, don't just press it flat.

11
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,200
Medicine, money, midnight luck — one bite.

12
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,600
Which would you fold first — pork or lamb?
